    {
      "title": "Flávio Bolsonaro flees Brazil, arrives in Miami following election defeat",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/flavio-bolsonaro-flees-brazil-arrives-in-miami-following-election-defeat-126102802096_1.html",
      "description": "Defeated Brazilian presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro and his family arrived in Miami on Wednesday after he refused to concede the election to President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and fled the country.\nIn a circuitous journey, Bolsonaro left for Argentina on Tuesday with his wife and two daughters, then travelled to Ecuador, according to Argentina officials and flight data. The 45-year-old senator, a close ally of US President Donald Trump, visited the White House in May, and the Trump administration approved US visas for him and his family this week.\nBolsonaro's father, Jair Bolsonaro, also fled to Florida after losing the 2022 presidential election to Lula before returning to Brazil three months later.\nFlavio Bolsonaro is under investigation by Brazil's Supreme Court, accused of corruption, money laundering and tax evasion. The court had ordered him to hand over his regular and diplomatic passports by noon Tuesday. It remained unclear whether he had complied, but allies said .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-29T03:50:56"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bolsonaro's son Flávio faces 'web of probes' in Brazil amid flight to Miami",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/bolsonaro-s-son-flavio-faces-web-of-probes-in-brazil-amid-flight-to-miami-126102900139_1.html",
      "description": "Flávio faces multiple probes in Brazil amid his mover to Miami via Argentina and Ecuador, while his brother Eduardo was convicted over alleged efforts to interfere in a probe against their father",
